entity spec_file                  # one .edda file; a fixture is one whole spec in one file
  name                            # order, for order.edda
  stories: many story, in order
  notes: many note, in order
  problems: many problem, in order      # every refusal and flag the rules of the reference,
                                        #   section 12, find in this file; ordered by line, then rule
  may create: agent
  may read:   agent, operator
  may update: agent
  may delete: nobody

entity note, part of spec_file    # one note: line, at any depth under a story
  text
  story_id
  line

story the checker refuses what it cannot read               # EDDA-001
  as an agent
  i want every line the grammar does not allow refused, with its line
    number and one plain message
  so that a file that passes has one reading and nothing hidden in it
  epic: CHK
  tags: checker, static
  note: EDDA-001 and EDDA-002 are the static checks of build step 1;
    links, versions, examples run, rules wrapped and done are later stories

  operation check(file: spec_file) returns file's problems
    who: agent, operator

  example a clean file has no problems
    given spec_file good from fixture order
    when  agent asks check(good) as found
    then  done
          found is []

  example an unknown keyword is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture unknown_keyword
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s kind is refused
          found[0]'s rule is unknown_keyword
          found[0]'s line is 19
          found[0]'s message is "unknown keyword: ensures"

  example an unknown name is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture unknown_name
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is unknown_name
          found[0]'s line is 17
          found[0]'s message is "unknown name: units_sold"

  example a tab is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture tab
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is tab
          found[0]'s line is 17
          found[0]'s message is "a tab; use two spaces"

  example an indent that is not two spaces is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture odd_indent
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is odd_indent
          found[0]'s line is 17
          found[0]'s message is "indent of 3 spaces; use a multiple of two"

  example a line that is not a sentence of the language is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture not_a_sentence
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is not_a_sentence
          found[0]'s line is 20
          found[0]'s message is "not a sentence of the language: set the order's status to removed"

  example a name declared twice is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture declared_twice
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is declared_twice
          found[0]'s line is 8
          found[0]'s message is "declared twice: units_sent"

  example a status not in its list is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture unknown_status
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is unknown_status
          found[0]'s line is 20
          found[0]'s message is "status not in its list: archived"

  example returns and ensure on one operation is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture returns_and_ensure
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is returns_and_ensure
          found[0]'s line is 16
          found[0]'s message is "returns and ensure on one operation: remove"

  example a story in the wrong file is refused
    given spec_file bad from fixture stock
    when  agent asks check(bad) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s rule is wrong_file
          found[0]'s line is 10
          found[0]'s message is "story FIX-001 belongs in order.edda"

story the checker flags what is allowed but doubtful        # EDDA-002
  as an operator
  i want a status nothing reaches and a story with no example shown as
    flags, not refusals
  so that the file still passes and I decide what to do
  epic: CHK
  tags: checker, static
  note: a question: on a done story is also a flag; it needs done, which
    needs links (a later story)

  example a status nothing reaches is flagged
    given spec_file odd from fixture unreachable_status
    when  agent asks check(odd) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s kind is flagged
          found[0]'s rule is unreachable_status
          found[0]'s line is 5
          found[0]'s message is "no change reaches status: delivered"

  example a story with no example is flagged
    given spec_file odd from fixture no_example
    when  agent asks check(odd) as found
    then  done
          count(found) is 1
          found[0]'s kind is flagged
          found[0]'s rule is no_example
          found[0]'s line is 10
          found[0]'s message is "story FIX-001 has no example"

story every note is collected in one place                  # EDDA-003
  as an operator
  i want every note: line across all files listed together, the same
    wording side by side
  so that a kind of note that keeps coming back shows itself
  epic: CHK
  tags: checker, backlog

  operation notes(files: many spec_file) returns
    [note for file in files for note in file's notes]
    ordered by text, then file name, then line
    who: agent, operator

  example notes from two files are listed with the same wording side by side
    given spec_file a from fixture notes_a
          spec_file b from fixture notes_b
    when  operator asks notes([a, b]) as all
    then  done
          count(all) is 4
          all[0]'s text is "a removed order keeps its history"
          all[1]'s text is "a workshop sees stock as of the last refresh"
          all[2]'s text is "the stock feed is refreshed every night"
          all[3]'s text is "the stock feed is refreshed every night"
          all[2]'s story_id is "FIX-001"
